# The `-baseline` variants and root-level SBOMs, from comparing a build against a
# published one. Same class as the four above, and they were missed because they are
# named after the comparison rather than after the tool.
/apko-baseline.lock.json
/packages-baseline/
/sbom-*.spdx.json

# Terraform state, ANYWHERE. test/crucible/.gitignore already covers the crucible's own
# directory and says why — a populated state file holds the RKE2 token, and it would hold
# the Hetzner API token and the S3 credentials with it. What it does not cover is a state
# file written somewhere else, and one duly appeared at the repo root: `terraform` writes
# state into the working directory it was invoked from, so running it one level up from
# where anyone expected leaves an uncovered file with everything in it. The root copy that
# prompted this rule was empty (0 resources, no outputs), so nothing leaked; the point is
# that nothing would have stopped it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
tfplan

# Python bytecode from hack/ scripts (check-dashboard-metrics.py).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
